---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Ask Ed a Question
permalink: /ask-ed/
description: Put a question to Edward Gregory, co-founder of EGregoRA. Answered publicly on the podcast or privately by letter.
---

<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">The Open Door</p>
  <h1>Ask Ed a Question</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">No question is too large, too small or too strange. Several are too urgent — see the note below.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap oracle-wrap reveal" id="oracle">
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="oracle-msg oracle-msg--oracle oracle-greet oracle-greet--lede">
      <p class="oracle-who">The Oracle</p>
      <div class="oracle-text">
        <p>Ask me anything inside the eleven limbs — or anything else at all. Cooking, grief, a
        gearbox, a bad week, a line of code: I will talk about it properly rather than steering you
        back to sacred geometry, and I will say I don't know when I don't. If a question needs
        today's news I will go and look it up and show you where I went, I will draw you a picture
        if you ask, and you can hand me a file to read and work from.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="fox-panel fox-panel--ask">
      <div class="fox-column">
      <div class="fox-side">
        <h3 class="fox-name">Gink</h3>
        <p class="muted small">Gink is the order's familiar, and he keeps its answers. Ask him here and he will
        read the reply aloud in his own voice; the words are the order's written ones, unchanged.</p>
        <p class="muted xsmall">He was Ed's fox. He died; the skull stayed, and sits on the desk within
        reach — a charm that feeds the connections and leans on him like an older part of his own soul.
        That the bone is there is fact; what it does is Ed's testimony, and we file it as such.</p>
        <p class="fox-controls">
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="fox-speak">Speak</button>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="fox-stop">Silence him</button>
        </p>
        <p class="muted xsmall" id="fox-status">Waking Gink…</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fox-stage" id="fox-stage" role="img"
           aria-label="Gink, a three-dimensional fox, the order's familiar, who reads the oracle's answers aloud"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="fox-ask">
    <form class="ornate oracle-form" id="oracle-form">
          <details class="oracle-opts">
            <summary>Name and limb (optional)</summary>
            <div class="grid two" style="gap:1rem">
              <div>
                <label for="o-name">Name</label>
                <input id="o-name" name="name" type="text" maxlength="80" placeholder="Rowan of the North">
              </div>
              <div>
                <label for="o-limb">Limb</label>
                <select id="o-limb" name="limb">
                  <option value="">Let the order decide</option>
                  <option>Cosmic physics &amp; astronomy</option>
                  <option>Druidry, trees &amp; nature</option>
                  <option>Sacred geometry</option>
                  <option>Astrology</option>
                  <option>Neuroscience &amp; psychology</option>
                  <option>Biology &amp; life</option>
                  <option>God, the Law of One &amp; contact</option>
                  <option>Magic &amp; the wizard's craft</option>
                  <option>The Black Tribunal</option>
                  <option>Alchemy &amp; the elemental forces</option>
                  <option>Consciousness</option>
                </select>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>

          <div class="oracle-files">
            <label class="btn btn--ghost file-btn">
              <span aria-hidden="true">⌁</span> Attach a file
              <input id="o-files" type="file" multiple
                     accept=".txt,.md,.markdown,.csv,.tsv,.json,.yaml,.yml,.xml,.html,.htm,.log,.srt,.vtt,.tex,.ini,.toml,.js,.py,.sql,.sh,.png,.jpg,.jpeg,.gif,.webp,text/*,image/*">
            </label>
            <ul class="file-list" id="o-file-list" aria-live="polite"></ul>
            <p class="muted xsmall">Notes, transcripts, data, a chapter, a photograph — up to 4&nbsp;MB each.
            Text is read and can be quoted, searched and argued with; images are kept as references. Export a
            PDF to text first. Anything you attach becomes part of this conversation and is stored with it, so
            do not send anything confidential.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="ask-actions">
            <button class="btn" type="submit" id="o-submit">Ask the Oracle</button>
            <button class="btn btn--mic" type="button" id="o-mic" hidden
                    aria-describedby="o-mic-hint">
              <span class="mic-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"
                     stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <rect x="9" y="2" width="6" height="12" rx="3"/>
                  <path d="M5 11a7 7 0 0 0 14 0"/>
                  <path d="M12 18v4M8.5 22h7"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="mic-label">Hold to speak</span>
              <span class="mic-waves" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            </button>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="o-reset" hidden>Begin again</button>
          </div>
          <p class="muted xsmall" id="o-mic-hint">Press and <strong>hold</strong> the microphone, ask your
          question out loud, then let go — the words are transcribed into the box below and sent to the order.
          Recognition happens in your browser; nothing is recorded or stored here. On a phone, hold with your
          thumb. Press <kbd>Space</kbd> while the button is focused to do the same thing.</p>

          <div class="ask-box">
            <label for="o-question">Your question</label>
            <textarea id="o-question" name="question" required maxlength="2000" rows="3"
              placeholder="Ask, then follow up — the oracle remembers the thread. Enter to send, Shift+Enter for a new line."></textarea>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="oracle-chat">
      <div class="oracle-bar">
        <p class="oracle-bar-note">A room to talk in — the oracle holds the whole thread, and will talk
        about anything, not only the limbs.</p>
        <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--small" type="button" id="o-expand"
                aria-pressed="false">Expand the space</button>
      </div>
      <div class="oracle-thread" id="oracle-thread" role="log" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Conversation with the oracle">
        <p class="oracle-waiting" id="oracle-waiting">The thread begins when you ask. Everything said
        stays here, in order.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="oracle-chips" id="oracle-chips">
        <button class="chip" type="button">Why 137.5 degrees and not 120?</button>
        <button class="chip" type="button">Is the Law of One testable?</button>
        <button class="chip" type="button">Did the druids really build Stonehenge?</button>
        <button class="chip" type="button">What does a psychedelic actually do to a brain?</button>
        <button class="chip" type="button">Is magic real, in one paragraph?</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="draw-box reveal" id="draw-box">
      <p class="kicker">ASK GINK TO DRAW</p>
      <h3>Make an Image</h3>
      <p class="muted small">Type what you want to see and Gink will draw it — photorealistic unless you
      ask for a painting, an engraving, a diagram or a cartoon. Made with FLUX.1-schnell, an open-weights
      model, so no company's key is required. Be specific: subject, setting, light, weather, lens, mood. A
      picture takes fifteen to forty seconds.</p>

      <form class="ornate draw-form" id="draw-form">
        <div>
          <label for="d-prompt">Your image</label>
          <textarea id="d-prompt" name="prompt" rows="3" maxlength="1200" required
            placeholder="A red fox standing in frosted bracken at first light, low winter sun behind it, breath visible on the cold air, shallow depth of field"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="draw-examples" id="draw-examples">
          <button class="chip" type="button">A dew-covered spider's web at dawn, each drop holding an inverted hedgerow</button>
          <button class="chip" type="button">An oak in a Somerset field under a full moon, long exposure, stars wheeling</button>
          <button class="chip" type="button">A brass orrery on a cluttered desk, candlelight, brass worn at the fingertips</button>
          <button class="chip" type="button">A copperplate engraving of the twelve zodiac glyphs around a wheel</button>
        </div>
        <div class="ask-actions">
          <button class="btn" type="submit" id="d-submit">Draw it</button>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="d-sketch-open"
                  aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="sketch-pad">Sketch it first</button>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="d-clear" hidden>Clear</button>
        </div>
      </form>

      <div class="sketch-pad" id="sketch-pad" hidden>
        <p class="muted small">Draw the arrangement you want &mdash; where things sit, how big they are,
        roughly what colour. Gink follows the composition, not the handwriting: the lines you put down are
        a plan, and the picture is rendered properly from them. Eight hundred pixels square.</p>

        <div class="sketch-tools" role="group" aria-label="Sketch tools">
          <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="Colour">
            <button class="swatch is-on" type="button" data-colour="#1b1b1f" aria-label="Near black"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#ffffff" aria-label="White"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#c8352f" aria-label="Red"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#d98c2b" aria-label="Orange"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#d7b05a" aria-label="Gold"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#5f9e58" aria-label="Green"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#2f6fa8" aria-label="Blue"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#7a4fa3" aria-label="Violet"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#8a5a33" aria-label="Brown"></button>
            <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#9a9aa2" aria-label="Grey"></button>
          </div>

          <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="Tool">
            <button class="tool is-on" type="button" data-tool="free">Freehand</button>
            <button class="tool" type="button" data-tool="line">Straight line</button>
            <button class="tool" type="button" data-tool="rect">Rectangle</button>
            <button class="tool" type="button" data-tool="ellipse">Ellipse</button>
            <button class="tool" type="button" data-tool="triangle">Triangle</button>
            <button class="tool" type="button" data-tool="fill">Fill area</button>
            <button class="tool" type="button" data-tool="erase">Eraser</button>
          </div>

          <div class="sketch-group sketch-group--size">
            <label for="sk-size">Pen</label>
            <input id="sk-size" type="range" min="1" max="60" step="1" value="4">
            <output id="sk-size-out" for="sk-size">4</output>
            <button class="tool" type="button" id="sk-solid" aria-pressed="false">Solid shapes</button>
          </div>

          <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="The sketch itself">
            <button class="tool" type="button" id="sk-undo">Undo</button>
            <button class="tool" type="button" id="sk-clear">Clear</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sketch-stage">
          <canvas id="sketch-canvas" width="800" height="800" role="img"
                  aria-label="A square sketching surface, eight hundred pixels across"></canvas>
        </div>

        <div class="ask-actions">
          <button class="btn" type="button" id="sk-use">Use this sketch</button>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="sk-close">Put it away</button>
        </div>
        <p class="auth-msg" id="sk-msg" role="status"></p>
      </div>


      <div class="byok">
        <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="bk-open"
                aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="byok-box">Use your own API</button>
        <div class="byok-box" id="byok-box" hidden>
          <p class="muted xsmall">Hold a key of your own? Hand it over for the picture and it is used
          once, here, for that request only &mdash; never written down, never logged, never kept after the
          image comes back. The order's own open-weights routes stay the default; this is simply a faster
          horse for anyone who has already paid for one.</p>

          <div class="byok-grid">
            <div>
              <label for="bk-provider">Provider</label>
              <select id="bk-provider">
                <option value="stability">Stability AI &middot; Stable Diffusion 3.5</option>
                <option value="openai">OpenAI, or anything that copies it</option>
                <option value="huggingface">Hugging Face Inference</option>
                <option value="replicate">Replicate</option>
                <option value="fal">fal.ai</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="bk-model">Model</label>
              <input id="bk-model" type="text" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
                     placeholder="sd3.5-large">
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="bk-key">Your key</label>
              <input id="bk-key" type="password" autocomplete="current-password"
                     spellcheck="false" placeholder="sk-&hellip;">
            </div>
            <div id="bk-base-wrap" hidden>
              <label for="bk-base">Base URL</label>
              <input id="bk-base" type="url" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
                     placeholder="https://api.openai.com">
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="byok-remember">
            <label class="check">
              <input id="bk-keep" type="checkbox">
              <span>Keep it in this tab until I close it</span>
            </label>
          </p>

          <div class="ask-actions">
            <button class="btn" type="button" id="bk-use">Use this key</button>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="bk-forget">Forget it</button>
          </div>
          <p class="auth-msg" id="bk-msg" role="status"></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="draw-out" id="draw-out" aria-live="polite"></div>

      <p class="muted xsmall">Every image here is <strong>generated, not photographed</strong>. It is a
      synthesis made to order and is never evidence of anything. Gink will not draw a real person in a
      situation they were never in, and nothing made here should be passed off as a record.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="draw-box film-box reveal" id="film-box">
      <p class="kicker">ASK GINK TO FILM</p>
      <h3>Make a Video</h3>
      <p class="muted small">Five seconds of 480p video from a sentence, made with
      <strong>HunyuanVideo 1.5</strong> — Tencent's open-weights model, 8.3 billion parameters, code and
      weights published. Describe motion: what moves, how the camera moves, the light. If the order's own
      GPU is doing the work the clip takes <strong>twenty minutes or more</strong>, because the model is
      fetched fresh each time; on a paid endpoint it is about three. Either way, leave the page open and
      it will appear below when it is done.</p>

      <div class="cont-strip" id="v-continues" hidden></div>

      <form class="ornate film-form" id="film-form">
        <div>
          <label for="v-prompt">Your clip</label>
          <textarea id="v-prompt" name="prompt" rows="3" maxlength="1200" required
            placeholder="Mist moving through a stand of oaks at dawn, slow dolly forward, shafts of low sun between the trunks, leaves turning in the draught"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="film-row">
          <div>
            <label for="v-model">Model</label>
            <select id="v-model" name="model">
              <option value="hunyuan15">HunyuanVideo 1.5 · 480p</option>
              <option value="wan22">Wan 2.2 · 480p</option>
              <option value="ltx">LTX-Video · fast</option>
              <option value="cogvideox">CogVideoX-5B</option>
              <option value="mochi">Mochi 1</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="v-aspect">Shape</label>
            <select id="v-aspect" name="aspect">
              <option value="16:9">Landscape · 16:9</option>
              <option value="9:16">Upright · 9:16</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="muted xsmall" id="v-model-note">Tencent, 8.3B. The house default: the best motion of
        the bunch.</p>
        <div class="draw-examples" id="film-examples">
          <button class="chip" type="button">A single candle flame guttering in a draught, close, dark background</button>
          <button class="chip" type="button">Ink dropped into still water, slow motion, backlit, blooming into filaments</button>
          <button class="chip" type="button">Clouds racing over a standing stone circle, time-lapse, long shadows turning</button>
        </div>
        <div class="ask-actions">
          <button class="btn" type="submit" id="v-submit">Generate</button>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="v-clear" hidden>Clear</button>
        </div>
      </form>

      <div class="draw-out" id="film-out" aria-live="polite"></div>


      <div class="keeper">
        <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--small" type="button" id="kp-open"
                aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="keeper-box">The keeper&rsquo;s key</button>
        <div class="keeper-box" id="keeper-box" hidden>
          <p class="muted xsmall">For whoever is minding the machines. The key opens a list of who asked
          for what, and the state of every GPU the order can reach &mdash; and lets the Kaggle lock be
          released when a job has died without saying so.</p>
          <form class="ornate keeper-form" id="keeper-form">
            <div class="keeper-row">
              <div>
                <label for="kp-pass">The key</label>
                <input id="kp-pass" name="pass" type="password" inputmode="numeric"
                       autocomplete="current-password" maxlength="40"
                       placeholder="&#9679;&#9679;&#9679;&#9679;">
              </div>
              <button class="btn" type="submit" id="kp-go">Open</button>
            </div>
          </form>
          <p class="auth-msg" id="kp-msg" role="status"></p>
          <div class="keeper-out" id="kp-out" hidden></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="muted xsmall">Every clip is <strong>generated, not filmed</strong>: nothing here records a
      real event, and it should never be presented as though it did. Video needs a GPU somewhere even when
      the model is open — if no video key is connected to this project, Gink will say so rather than
      pretend.</p>
    </div>

<div class="draw-box model-box reveal" id="model-box">
      <p class="kicker">THE TURNING SHOP</p>
      <h3>Make a 3D Model</h3>
      <p class="muted small">Build a thing out of solids. Add a box, a sphere, a cylinder, a cone or a
      torus; move it, turn it, scale it, colour it, and the piece assembles in the window below. It is
      deliberately simple &mdash; blocks and primitives, the way a model is roughed out before it is
      sculpted. Nothing is sent anywhere: the whole shop runs in this page. When you are done, take the
      model away as an <strong>OBJ</strong> file any 3D program will open, or hand the view to Gink and
      let him render it as a photograph.</p>

      <div class="model-stage" id="model-stage" role="img"
           aria-label="A three-dimensional workspace showing the model being built"></div>

      <div class="model-tools">
        <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="Add a solid">
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="box">Box</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="sphere">Sphere</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="cylinder">Cylinder</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="cone">Cone</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" data-add="torus">Torus</button>
        </div>
        <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="Colour">
          <button class="swatch is-on" type="button" data-colour="#d7b05a" aria-label="Gold"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#b8c0cc" aria-label="Steel"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#8a5a33" aria-label="Wood"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#5f9e58" aria-label="Green"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#2f6fa8" aria-label="Blue"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#c8352f" aria-label="Red"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#1b1b1f" aria-label="Near black"></button>
          <button class="swatch" type="button" data-colour="#efe3c8" aria-label="Bone"></button>
        </div>
        <div class="sketch-group" role="group" aria-label="The piece">
          <button class="tool" type="button" id="md-duplicate">Duplicate</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" id="md-delete">Delete</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" id="md-clear">Clear all</button>
          <button class="tool" type="button" id="md-grid" aria-pressed="true">Grid</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="model-sliders" id="model-sliders" hidden>
        <div class="model-slider">
          <label for="md-x">Left &amp; right</label>
          <input id="md-x" type="range" min="-6" max="6" step="0.05" value="0">
        </div>
        <div class="model-slider">
          <label for="md-y">Up &amp; down</label>
          <input id="md-y" type="range" min="-3" max="8" step="0.05" value="0">
        </div>
        <div class="model-slider">
          <label for="md-z">Near &amp; far</label>
          <input id="md-z" type="range" min="-6" max="6" step="0.05" value="0">
        </div>
        <div class="model-slider">
          <label for="md-scale">Size</label>
          <input id="md-scale" type="range" min="0.1" max="4" step="0.02" value="1">
        </div>
        <div class="model-slider">
          <label for="md-turn">Turn</label>
          <input id="md-turn" type="range" min="0" max="360" step="1" value="0">
        </div>
        <div class="model-slider">
          <label for="md-tilt">Tilt</label>
          <input id="md-tilt" type="range" min="-180" max="180" step="1" value="0">
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="muted xsmall" id="md-status">Add a solid to begin. Click a solid to select it; drag the
      background to turn the view, and scroll to come closer.</p>

      <div class="ask-actions">
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="md-export">Take the model away (OBJ)</button>
        <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="md-render">Render this view as a photograph</button>
      </div>
      <p class="auth-msg" id="md-msg" role="status"></p>

      <p class="muted xsmall">The OBJ file carries the shapes and their positions; colours are written
      alongside it in the same download as an MTL. Rendering hands the current view to the image
      generator as a sketch, so the photograph follows the arrangement you built rather than a
      description of it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="draw-box montage-box reveal" id="montage-box">
      <p class="kicker">THE CUTTING ROOM</p>
      <h3>Make a Montage</h3>
      <p class="muted small">Every clip <em>and every picture</em> you generate on this page is collected
      here. Put them in order, trim the ends or set how long a still holds, choose a cut or a crossfade,
      and the page will edit them into one film — rendered in
      your own browser, with no upload and no service in the middle. The result downloads as a single
      file. Clips made before you cleared the page are not kept; this is a cutting room, not an archive.</p>

      <ul class="shot-list" id="shot-list" aria-live="polite">
        <li class="shot-empty">No shots yet. Draw a picture or film a clip above and it lands here — then any shot can be continued from, so the next one keeps the same characters.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="film-row">
        <div>
          <label for="m-transition">Between shots</label>
          <select id="m-transition" name="transition">
            <option value="cut">Straight cut</option>
            <option value="0.5">Crossfade · half a second</option>
            <option value="1">Crossfade · one second</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="m-shape">Shape</label>
          <select id="m-shape" name="shape">
            <option value="854x480">Landscape · 854 × 480</option>
            <option value="480x854">Upright · 480 × 854</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ask-actions">
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="m-render" disabled>Edit the montage</button>
        <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" id="m-clear" hidden>Empty the room</button>
      </div>
      <p class="auth-msg" id="m-msg" role="status"></p>
      <div class="montage-out" id="montage-out"></div>

      <p class="muted xsmall">The edit happens frame by frame on a canvas in this page and is recorded as
      it plays, so a two-minute montage takes two minutes to make. Nothing is sent anywhere. For anything
      more ambitious — narration, music, titles, stock footage, a real timeline —
      <a href="https://github.com/calesthio/OpenMontage" rel="noopener">OpenMontage</a> is installed in
      this repository under <code>openmontage/</code>; see the README there.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="muted xsmall oracle-foot">Test everything kindly. If an answer cannot survive your scepticism,
    it does not deserve your belief — and the written form below reaches Ed himself.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦ ✦ ✦</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Write to Ed directly</h3>
      <form class="ornate" id="letter-form">
        <div>
          <label for="name">Your name or chosen name</label>
          <input id="name" name="name" type="text" required placeholder="Rowan of the North">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="email">Email (so Ed can reply)</label>
          <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required placeholder="you@example.com">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="topic">Which limb does this belong to?</label>
          <select id="topic" name="topic">
            <option>Cosmic physics &amp; astronomy</option>
            <option>Druidry, trees &amp; nature</option>
            <option>Sacred geometry</option>
            <option>Astrology</option>
            <option>Neuroscience &amp; psychology</option>
            <option>Biology &amp; life</option>
            <option>God, the Law of One &amp; contact</option>
            <option>Magic &amp; the wizard's craft</option>
            <option>History, propaganda &amp; the shadow</option>
            <option>Something that fits nowhere</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="question">Your question</label>
          <textarea id="question" name="question" required placeholder="Ask plainly. Ed would rather have the real question than the polite one."></textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="public">May we answer this publicly?</label>
          <select id="public" name="public">
            <option>Yes — use my name</option>
            <option>Yes — but keep me anonymous</option>
            <option>No — private reply only</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label for="website">Leave this empty</label>
          <input id="website" name="website" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
        </div>
        <div class="captcha" data-captcha="letter">
          <p class="captcha-label">Read the gate-word and type it back</p>
          <div class="captcha-row">
            <div class="captcha-art" data-captcha-art aria-live="polite"></div>
            <button class="captcha-new" type="button" data-captcha-new
                    title="Draw another word" aria-label="Draw another gate-word">&#8634;</button>
          </div>
          <input type="text" data-captcha-input autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="characters"
                 spellcheck="false" maxlength="8" required
                 aria-label="The gate-word" placeholder="The five letters above">
        </div>
        <button class="btn" type="submit" id="letter-send">Send the Question</button>
        <p class="auth-msg" id="letter-msg" role="status"></p>
        <p class="form-note">Your letter is stored, forwarded to Ed, and acknowledged by return of post —
        the acknowledgement arrives within a minute and carries a reference you can quote. If nothing
        appears, check the spam fold, or write to
        <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> directly.</p>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="frame mb-2">
        <h2>How Ed Answers</h2>
        <ul class="biblio">
          <li>Every question is read. Most are answered within a fortnight.</li>
          <li>The best are answered at length in the <a href="/podcast/">podcast mailbag</a>.</li>
          <li>Ed will tell you plainly when he does not know — that is the most common answer, and the most useful.</li>
          <li>Where evidence exists, you get the evidence. Where only tradition exists, you get told it is tradition.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="frame caution">
        <p><strong>Please read.</strong> EGregoRA is a study order, not a clinic. Ed cannot give medical,
        psychiatric, legal or financial advice, and will not advise on taking any controlled substance. If you
        are in crisis, please contact your local emergency service or a crisis line
        (UK: Samaritans, 116 123, free, 24 hours) rather than waiting for a reply here.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="frame mt-2">
        <h3>Questions Already in the Pile</h3>
        <details class="scroll"><summary>Is astrology real?</summary>
          <p>Real as a symbolic system with four millennia of continuous use and enormous cultural weight — yes,
          demonstrably. Real as a physical force by which Saturn's position alters your week — no; every
          controlled test of that claim has failed. Both halves of that sentence matter.</p></details>
        <details class="scroll"><summary>Does the Law of One hold up?</summary>
          <p>As cosmology, it is untestable. As philosophy, its core — that consciousness is unitary and that free
          will is sacred — sits in good company with Advaita Vedanta, Plotinus and Whitehead. Read it as a text, not
          a transcript, and it becomes much more interesting.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

